# interface_attrs_179.py
# Modular interface XML bodies for Cisco-IOS-XE-native (IOS XE 17.9),
# derived from Cisco-IOS-XE-interfaces rev 2022-07-01 (module-version 10.0.0),
# Cisco-IOS-XE-switch rev 2022-07-01 (5.0.0), Cisco-IOS-XE-vlan rev 2022-03-01 (4.0.0),
# Cisco-IOS-XE-native rev 2022-07-01 (10.0.0).
# Same conventions as interface_attrs_1715.py — same label names, _179 suffix.
# Placeholders use $…; NS dict supplies $N, $NC, $SW, $ST, $VLAN.
#
# DESIGN RULES (modular / operational):
#   * Valued leaves (true|false) are symmetric: caller passes $flag.
#   * Every presence leaf has a matching *_REMOVE_179 twin.
#   * Every additive/list feature has a *_REMOVE_179 (remove-by-key) twin.
#   * Bulk forms accept $*_block fragments so the engine controls contents.
#   * Interface scaffolding (<interfaces><$parent><$name>) is owned by
#     the caller's wrapper — bodies here are bare interface-scoped nodes.
#   * Families that exist in 17.15 but not here are registered with
#     _t() in TEMPLATES and explained in NOT_PRESENT.
#
# 17.9 DIFFERENCES vs the 1715 templates (all verified against the YANG):
#   * L2PT drop/shutdown-threshold: per-protocol leaf IS the pps value (uint16);
#     `packet-rate` is a sibling leaf, not a child  -> templates reshaped.
#   * HOLD_QUEUE_REMOVE: list entry removal needs the key.
#   * KEEPALIVE: no <keepalive-config>; uses choice keepalive | keepalive-settings.
#   * IP4_URPF: no ACL leaf under verify/unicast/source  -> $acl_block dropped.
#   * IP4_ARP_INSPECT_RATE: no burst leaf  -> $burst_block dropped.
#   * IP4_PROXY_ARP / REDIRECTS / CLEAR_DF: closing </ip> present here.
#   * PQ_COS_MAP is a container (one per interface), not a list.
#   * NEGOTIATION exists only on lists ucse and Ethernet-Internal.
#   * PHY_MEDIA_TYPE: Gig/2.5G/5G/10G/25G/40G/50G + AppGig lists only.
#   * PHY_FEC: TwentyFiveGigE list only.
#   * Port-channel uses <load-balancing> (vlan|flow); no load-balance-hash-algo.
#
# SWITCH-MODULE NOTES (Cisco-IOS-XE-switch 5.0.0):
#   * Everything under switchport-config/switchport and interface-level `macsec`
#     carries xmlns="$SW" on the first node.
#   * L2_PORTSEC_MAX / MAX_VLAN: list `maxcount` (key max-addresses, leaf vlan).
#   * L2_PORTSEC_MAC_STICKY: hw-address-access with leaf sticky='sticky'.
#   * MSEC_ENABLE: plain <macsec/> leaf, not <macsec-enable><macsec/>.
#   * PVLAN_GLOBAL*/PVLAN_SECONDARY*: native-scoped (wrap with wrap_native()).

